-- Row il-73. EXPECTED RED: two assertions that fail on purpose, one per item. Each says what the citing words reach is untouched by the deposited instruments, and each is FALSE.
-- I1: no enactment named in section 4A(b)(2) is repealed, in whole or in part, by an instrument deposited here.
--     False: SH 2708 section 358 prints the Bankruptcy Ordinance as repealed but for one section, and section 359 items (4) and (5) print sections 195 to 201 and chapters yod-alef to yod-zayin of the Companies Ordinance as repealed (two enactments).
-- I2: the chapter number written in section 11 for the cited chapter is the number the 1995 print deposited here gives that chapter.
--     False: the written number is ג׳2, and the table of the 1995 print gives the chapter whose 1968 entry is ג׳2 the number ו׳ in its 1995 column.
-- The count, two, is declared in check.sh (expected_failed) and in encoding.json (expected_red). If a later instrument or print changes one of these, its assertion turns green and the declared count must go down with it.

§ `Expected red`

#ASSERT `no enactment the citing words name is repealed in whole or in part` `item I1: section 4A(b)(2) names two enactments`
